  ('aa827693-dc8d-48f6-bfd8-5ec40311ed48','Gun World and Archery Pro Shop in Corydon, Indiana combines firearms retail with a dedicated archery pro shop, serving southern Indiana''s hunting community just across the Ohio River from Louisville. Having archery gear, arrows, sights, and tuning support available alongside general hunting supplies makes it a convenient single stop for local bowhunters gearing up before deer season rather than needing a specialty archery-only shop. Details on whether the location also offers a shooting range or lessons aren''t listed here, so archers in the Corydon area should contact the shop directly to confirm what services and range access are currently available.'),
  ('3f8831b8-cd25-4716-9864-cbbe26a9fc3b','GUNTRY in Owings Mills, Maryland is a commercial archery operation just northwest of Baltimore, offering both a pro shop and lessons on site. That pairing means someone new to the sport can get outfitted with a bow and immediately book instruction rather than having to source gear and coaching from separate places, a useful setup for Baltimore-area families and first-time shooters. It positions GUNTRY as more of a learn-to-shoot destination than a bare-bones range, well suited to beginners working on fundamentals before moving toward leagues or hunting prep. Contact GUNTRY directly for current lesson packages and shop hours.'),
  ('23c8a981-f77b-46f7-8768-c6a5bb199036','Halls Arrow is a volunteer-run archery club based in Manchester, Connecticut, part of the greater Hartford area. Being member-operated rather than commercial, its range access and shoot schedule tend to follow the group''s own calendar rather than standard retail hours. No further detail on course type or programs is listed here, so archers in the Manchester or Hartford area curious about shooting with this club should reach out directly to ask about membership, dues, and whether the range is open to guests looking to try archery before committing to join.'),
  ('7caea186-6e79-4598-8025-10fd0c03575f','Hampton Hills Metro Park Archery Range is a public archery facility within the Summit Metro Parks system in Akron, Ohio, giving local residents free or low-cost access to a range without needing a club membership. Public park ranges like this are typically the easiest entry point for someone in the area who wants to try archery casually or practice between hunting seasons, since they don''t require joining an organization first. Specific hours, target setup, and whether equipment rental is available aren''t listed here, so visitors should check with Summit Metro Parks directly before heading out to Hampton Hills.'),
  ('7f3feca6-662f-4a3c-9568-e6d29079d3a2','Harford Bowmen is an archery club based in Havre de Grace, Maryland, at the mouth of the Susquehanna River in Harford County. As a club, it gives area archers a shared range and membership structure rather than commercial walk-in access. There''s a related incorporated entity also operating under a similar name in the same town, so anyone reaching out should confirm which listing they''re contacting. Course details, shoot schedule, and membership terms aren''t listed here, so archers in the Havre de Grace area interested in joining should contact Harford Bowmen directly for current information before planning a visit.'),
  ('0e7ad46d-c3eb-4682-a78e-61633c0d39e0','Harford Bowmen Inc is the incorporated, volunteer-run version of the Harford Bowmen name operating in Havre de Grace, Maryland. Structuring as a formal nonprofit entity typically means the club owns or leases its range property and runs on a member board rather than informal organization, common for longer-established archery clubs in Harford County. No specific detail on course layout, lane count, or open-shoot hours is listed here, so archers in the Havre de Grace area should contact Harford Bowmen Inc directly to confirm current membership requirements, dues, and range access before visiting.'),
  ('d4a38603-91fe-4fd7-9e33-0741139042f8','Harrisburg Archery Club serves the Pennsylvania capital region, giving local archers a volunteer-run home range in Harrisburg. Member-operated clubs like this typically keep costs low for shooters while relying on the membership itself to maintain the range and set the shoot calendar. No specific details on course type, indoor or outdoor setup, or current programs are listed here, so anyone in the greater Harrisburg area interested in archery should reach out to the club directly to ask about membership dues, open-shoot times, and whether visitors can come try the range before joining.'),
  ('71570d40-eadb-4b94-bdeb-6f64da76fdcf','Hartford Gun Club, despite its name, is located in East Granby, Connecticut, north of the city it''s named for, and offers archery as one of its shooting-sports disciplines. Clubs organized around general gun-club membership often treat archery as a complementary activity alongside firearms shooting, which can mean shared facilities and a combined membership fee. Specific detail on the archery range''s course type and available hours isn''t listed here, so archers in the greater Hartford area interested in shooting with this club should contact Hartford Gun Club directly to confirm archery-specific access and current scheduling.'),
  ('a3dcb6ba-d6dd-4815-85e7-23cf615125f1','Harvard Sportsmen''s Club is a volunteer-run outdoor recreation club based in Harvard, Massachusetts, in the rural northern part of Worcester County. Clubs like this commonly offer archery alongside other shooting sports for their membership, with the range maintained by the members themselves rather than paid staff. No specific detail on course format, lane setup, or public access is listed here, so archers in the greater Fitchburg or Route 2 corridor area interested in shooting with this club should reach out directly to ask about membership requirements, dues, and whether the archery range is open to prospective members for a trial visit.'),
  ('162ad43b-e1a1-4c5c-bfe1-e18eb6ba176d','Harwinton Rod & Gun Club serves the small Litchfield County town of Harwinton, Connecticut, offering archery as part of a broader rod-and-gun club roster that typically includes fishing and firearms activities alongside bow shooting. That combined-club model is common in rural Connecticut, giving members one membership for multiple outdoor pursuits rather than a standalone archery-only operation. Specific detail on the archery range''s course type, hours, and current programs isn''t listed here, so archers in the Litchfield Hills area interested in shooting with this club should contact Harwinton Rod & Gun Club directly to confirm access and membership terms.')
) AS v(id, description)
WHERE r.id = v.id::uuid AND r.is_claimed = false;
